.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt MTKBTFW 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mtkbtfw
.Nd firmware download utility for MediaTek MT79xx chip based Bluetooth
USB devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl d Ar device_name
.Fl f Ar firmware_path
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility downloads the matching firmware patch to the specified
.Xr ugen 4
device and turns on its Bluetooth function.
.Pp
This utility will
.Em only
work with MediaTek MT7920, MT7921, MT7902, MT7922 and MT7925 chip based
Bluetooth USB devices.
These controllers start in a boot ROM that refuses standard HCI commands,
so
.Xr ng_ubt 4
does not attach to them until
.Nm
has run.
The identification is based on the USB vendor ID/product ID pair.
.Pp
The
.Nm
utility reads the chip ID and ROM version from the device to pick the
firmware image, which is looked up below
.Ar firmware_path
using the same file names and
.Pa mt7925/
subdirectory as the
.Pa mediatek/
directory of the linux-firmware repository, for example
.Pa mt7925/BT_RAM_CODE_MT7925_1_1_hdr.bin .
Sections the chip reports as already loaded are skipped.
After a successful download the device is reset so that
.Xr ng_ubt 4
can attach; the patch survives that reset.
If the controller already accepts HCI commands,
.Nm
exits without touching it.
.Pp
.Xr devd 8
runs
.Nm
automatically when a supported device is attached, using
.Pa /usr/local/share/mtkbt-firmware
as the firmware path.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl D
Enable verbose debugging.
.It Fl d Ar device_name
Specify
.Xr ugen 4
device name.
.It Fl I
Enable informational debugging.
.It Fl f Ar firmware_path
Specify the directory containing the firmware files to search and upload.
.It Fl h
Display usage message and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /etc/devd/mtkbtfw.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/devd/mtkbtfw.conf
.Xr devd 8
rules that run
.Nm .
.It Pa /usr/local/share/mtkbt-firmware
Default firmware directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libusb 3 ,
.Xr ng_ubt 4 ,
.Xr ugen 4 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr iwmbtfw 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Mx 4.2 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.Nm
is based on the
.Xr iwmbtfw 8
utility and on the MediaTek ISC-licensed Linux btmtk driver source code.
It is written by
.An Lucas Holt Aq Mt luke@foolishgames.com .
.Sh BUGS
Only the MT7925 has been tested.
MT7663, MT7668, MT6639 and MT7935 based devices are not supported.
